From e96f6900bb2fe689df040380b98b5f6315d37c16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soulexit <metehan.tanriverdi01@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:56:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] panvk/bifrost: robust indexed-indirect index range,
 copy-shader guard, fault tooling

- Clamp firstIndex/indexCount of batched indexed indirect draws to the
  bound index buffer in the GPU min/max scan and patch kernels.
- vk_meta buffer-to-image copy: discard fragments whose copy coordinates
  are negative; the 32-bit buffer offset otherwise wraps ~4 GiB past the
  buffer.
- PANVK_VALIDATE now also checks fragment jobs (FBD, frame shader DCDs,
  render target words), varyings, full texture surface tables and the
  descriptor-copy set addresses; on a failed submission it dumps the
  draws of the batches that stopped (descriptors + shader binaries) next
  to the driver, and logs which emulated draw paths an app reaches.
- PANVK_KBASE_NO_DEFER, PANVK_NO_CPU_INDEX_SCAN: bisect switches.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
